# Bug Bounty — ROUTER

> **This SKILL.md is a lightweight router.** Content lives in split files below.
> Agent MUST load the correct split file per phase.
> 
> **⚠️ NEVER load all skills at once.** Use the phased matrix below.

> **Reconciling "use ALL skills and tools" with phased loading.** The operator's standing
> kickoff is *"pakai semua skill dan tools yg ada, lalu periksa target X, cari dari segala
> sisi, tanpa kecuali, termasuk bisnis logicnya."* Read that as **full COVERAGE across the
> whole run**, never as "load every skill simultaneously". The budget table below is
> absolute: loading everything at once triggers context compression, skills get pruned
> mid-run, and the audit dies with nothing to show. Full coverage is delivered by working
> the phased matrix to completion and then publishing the **TOOL-COVERAGE LEDGER** (stop
> rule 23) that proves every tool ran — coverage is demonstrated by the ledger, not by
> how many skills were opened. Same reading applies to the sub-skills: load the one that
> governs the phase you are in, then evict.
> 
> **⚡ FEATURE-ABUSE DOCTRINE (operator, 2026-10-29) — 4 hard gates, EVERY audit.** Full text:
> `redteam-mindset` → **Part 3**; enforced at 0A by `bb-audit-launcher`. Short form:
> **(1)** start from features that work *as designed* — name the INVARIANT and the *impossible
> state* you want, never a vuln-class list; **(2)** hunt the interaction, not the feature
> (create-in-A/change-in-B, low-role→high-role endpoint, cross-tenant identifier, inter-feature
> race) and re-test every candidate against ≥2 features sharing the object/state; **(3)** symptom
> → handler → the guard that never ran, then grep that root estate-wide and test EVERY twin
> (one root = one class = one report); **(4)** status code is not proof — prove with a state diff
> (re-read, side effects, other actor's view, downstream list/search/export); **(5) compose the Low
> pool** — label every Low K/A/B/X (Knowledge/Action/Bypass/Amplifier), find the edges, name the
> terminal sink, prove end-to-end 3x from a clean session, then submit ONE chain report whose severity
> is what the chain reaches (never the sum of parts, never five separate Lows). Procedure:
> `chain-to-impact` -> "Multi-Low composition"; doctrine `redteam-mindset` 3.5. Failing any gate = NOT reportable.
